---
/**
 * Right column: live model result.
 *
 * The actual content of `#result-ml` is rendered by calculator.ts whenever
 * the form changes (showProbability / showError / hideResult). The wrapping
 * panel stays in the DOM so the column has consistent dimensions even when
 * no result is available yet.
 *
 * The column is intentionally chromeless — no card, border, or background.
 * showProbability renders two stacked blocks:
 *   1. Familial Hypercholesterolemia — Yes / No, coloured by the verdict.
 *   2. Estimated Likelihood — a probability gauge with a tick at the
 *      screening threshold and the predicted probability label underneath.
 *      Hovering the gauge surfaces the exact threshold percentage and
 *      specificity via the native title tooltip; a paragraph beneath
 *      explains how the threshold was chosen.
 *
 * The error state reuses the same eyebrow style; the verdict line carries
 * the validation message in red.
 */
---

<aside class="result-panel" id="result-panel">
  <div class="section-head">Prediction</div>
  <div id="result-ml" class="result-box result-box--hidden"></div>
  <p class="result-panel__placeholder" id="result-placeholder">
    Fill in the required fields to estimate the likelihood of familial hypercholesterolaemia.
  </p>
</aside>
